("54","Protocols & Structural Typing","Learn the idea behind structural typing: code can depend on behavior instead of one concrete class hierarchy.","This is useful for flexible libraries and testable architecture.","Define a protocol-like interface for objects that can save data.","Adding abstractions before you have a real need for them.","Swap a real repository for a fake test repository."),
("55","Itertools","Use itertools tools such as chain, islice, product, combinations, and groupby for efficient iteration.","The standard library already solves many iteration problems elegantly.","Generate combinations of project features without nested loops.","Forgetting that some iterators are consumed as you iterate.","Build a tiny combination generator."),
("56","Collections Module","Use Counter, defaultdict, deque, and named structures when ordinary lists and dictionaries are awkward.","Choosing the right standard-library structure can simplify code dramatically.","Count words with Counter and build a queue with deque.","Using a complicated custom structure for a simple problem.","Replace one manual counting loop with Counter."),
