("63","Concurrency: Threads vs Processes","Understand the practical difference between threads, processes, and asynchronous I/O.","The right concurrency model depends on whether work is I/O-bound or CPU-bound.","Classify ten example workloads by the best concurrency model.","Assuming more workers always means more performance.","Benchmark a small I/O task with a few worker counts."),
