("70","Flask Forms & Validation","Validate form input, handle errors, preserve user experience, and keep server-side validation authoritative.","Browser validation is useful but never the security boundary.","Build a registration form with server-side validation.","Trusting hidden fields or client-side checks.","Return field-specific errors without leaking sensitive details."),
("71","Sessions, Cookies & CSRF","Understand sessions, cookie flags, CSRF tokens, and why state-changing requests need protection.","Web authentication depends on secure state management.","Explain why HttpOnly, SameSite, Secure, and CSRF each exist.","Treating a cookie as proof that every request is trustworthy.","Threat-model a login form and its state-changing actions."),
