("73","Web Security Fundamentals","Learn XSS, SQL injection, CSRF, open redirects, insecure file handling, and least privilege at a practical level.","Knowing common attack classes changes how you design input and output.","Find the unsafe line in a deliberately vulnerable example.","Assuming escaping alone solves every web security problem.","Create a checklist for a small Flask application."),
("74","REST API Design","Design predictable resources, HTTP methods, status codes, validation, pagination, and error responses.","A clean API is easier for browsers, mobile apps, and other services to consume.","Design endpoints for courses, lessons, and progress.","Returning a different response shape for every endpoint.","Write an API contract for one resource."),
