("76","Caching & Performance","Learn what to cache, cache invalidation basics, database query costs, and measuring before optimizing.","Performance work should be driven by evidence rather than guesses.","Identify one expensive operation and define a useful metric.","Adding caching before knowing whether anything is slow.","Measure a route before and after one targeted optimization."),
("77","Python Profiling","Use time measurements and profilers to locate slow functions instead of optimizing by intuition.","Profiling turns performance debugging into an evidence-based process.","Profile a deliberately slow list-processing function.","Optimizing code that is not a real bottleneck.","Write down the bottleneck, hypothesis, change, and result."),
("78","Clean Architecture in Practice","Use boundaries and small modules to keep a project understandable without creating needless abstraction.","Architecture should make change safer, not make simple code harder to read.","Split a mini app into domain, persistence, and interface layers.","Creating ten layers for a fifty-line script.","Refactor one feature while keeping its tests unchanged."),
("79","Command-Line Interfaces","Build polished CLIs with arguments, subcommands, validation, exit codes, and helpful output.","CLI tools are a practical way to turn Python into reusable software.","Design a course-progress CLI with list and mark-complete commands.","Printing errors but still returning success exit codes.","Make invalid input produce a useful message and non-zero exit."),
("80","Automation with Scheduling","Combine Python scripts with scheduling concepts for recurring reports, cleanup, backups, or reminders.","Automation becomes powerful when it is reliable and observable.","Design a daily report job that can safely run twice.","Assuming scheduled jobs always run exactly once.","Make a job idempotent and log its result."),
